{
  "root_node": "model.stg_orders",
  "cause": "code_change",
  "action": "patch",
  "evidence": "The stg_orders model selects o_orderdate directly as order_date, preserving its VARCHAR type. The contract for stg_orders requires order_date to be DATE, causing a compilation error. Profiling raw.orders.o_orderdate shows it is VARCHAR but can be losslessly converted to DATE using format %m/%d/%Y (15000 rows, 0 failures, lossless). Therefore the issue is the model's SQL not applying the required conversion, not upstream data. Updating the model to cast order_date (e.g., strptime(trim(o_orderdate), '%m/%d/%Y')::date) will satisfy the contract."
}
